  "learningBlocks": [
    {
      "id": "l31-b1",
      "type": "concept",
      "title": "Questions have their own signal words",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "By Lesson 31, the difficulty is rarely basic case recognition. The problem is identifying what kind of word you are seeing: interrogative quis/quid, indefinite aliquis, negative nemo, or a question particle such as numquid or nonne.",
        "fr": "À la leçon 31, la difficulté n'est plus le simple repérage des cas. Il faut identifier la nature du mot : interrogatif quis/quid, indéfini aliquis, négatif nemo, ou particule interrogative comme numquid ou nonne."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-plater-white-1926",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l31-b2",
      "type": "contrast",
      "title": "numquid and nonne are not interchangeable",
      "sourceId": "vulg-jn6-68-l31",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Question particles carry pragmatic expectation. numquid can suggest doubt or an expected negative; nonne normally invites confirmation. Translate the question naturally after reading its force.",
        "fr": "Les particules interrogatives portent une attente pragmatique. numquid peut suggérer le doute ou une réponse négative ; nonne appelle normalement la confirmation. Traduisez naturellement après avoir reconnu cette force."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "vulg-jn6-68-l31",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-plater-white-1926",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l31-b3",
      "type": "authentic-example",
      "title": "Quid quaeritis?",
      "sourceId": "vulg-lk24-5-l31",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "quid is not merely a dictionary word 'what': its form and clause role matter. Here it functions inside the direct question governed by quaeritis.",
        "fr": "quid n'est pas seulement le mot de dictionnaire « quoi » : sa forme et sa fonction comptent. Ici il appartient à la question directe régie par quaeritis."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "vulg-lk24-5-l31",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-plater-white-1926",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l31-b4",
      "type": "indefinite",
      "title": "quis can become indefinite",
      "sourceId": "vulg-mt16-24-l31",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "After si, quis commonly has indefinite force: 'if anyone'. This is why a reader must recognize context, not mechanically translate every quis as a direct question.",
        "fr": "Après si, quis prend couramment une valeur indéfinie : « si quelqu'un ». Il faut donc lire le contexte, non traduire mécaniquement tout quis comme une question directe."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "vulg-mt16-24-l31",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-plater-white-1926",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l31-b5",
      "type": "irregular",
      "title": "Irregular high-frequency verbs must be recognized whole",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "volo, nolo, fero and iubeo occur too often to parse as exceptions from scratch. Learn their common forms as reader vocabulary and then analyze tense/person normally.",
        "fr": "volo, nolo, fero et iubeo sont trop fréquents pour être redécouverts comme exceptions à chaque occurrence. Apprenez leurs formes courantes comme vocabulaire de lecteur, puis analysez normalement temps et personne."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-plater-white-1926",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l31-b6",
      "type": "retrieval",
      "title": "The final pronoun spiral",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "The pronoun system is now complete enough for ordinary Church-Latin reading. The task is family selection plus case/function—not memorizing another isolated table.",
        "fr": "Le système pronominal est désormais assez complet pour la lecture ordinaire du latin ecclésiastique. Le travail consiste à choisir la famille puis le cas et la fonction, non à mémoriser encore un tableau isolé."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-plater-white-1926",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    }
  ],
